      "text": "love the Lord thy God with all thy heart … and with all thy mind, Matt. 22:37. see him that was possessed with the devil … in his right mind, Mark 5:15. received the word with … readiness of mind, Acts 17:11. God gave them over to a reprobate mind, Rom. 1:28. another law in my members, warring against the law of my mind, Rom. 7:23. carnal mind is enmity against God, Rom. 8:7. knoweth what is the mind of the Spirit, Rom. 8:27. who hath known the mind of the Lord, Rom. 11:34. transformed by the renewing of your mind, Rom. 12:2. every man be fully persuaded in his own mind, Rom. 14:5. perfectly joined together in the same mind, 1 Cor. 1:10. we have the mind of Christ, 1 Cor. 2:16. their minds were blinded, 2 Cor. 3:14. hath blinded the minds of them which believe not, 2 Cor. 4:4. there be first a willing mind, 2 Cor. 8:12. be of one mind, live in peace, 2 Cor. 13:11. walk not as … Gentiles … in the vanity of their mind, Eph. 4:17. renewed in the spirit of your mind, Eph. 4:23. with one mind striving together for the faith, Philip. 1:27. same love, being … of one mind, Philip. 2:2. That ye be not soon shaken in mind, 2 Thes. 2:2. God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but … of a sound mind, 2 Tim. 1:7. resist the truth: men of corrupt minds, 2 Tim. 3:8. even their mind and conscience is defiled, Titus 1:15. without thy mind would I do nothing, Philem. 1:14. put my laws into their mind, Heb. 8:10 (10:16). lest ye be wearied and faint in your minds, Heb. 12:3. gird up the loins of your mind, 1 Pet. 1:13. be ye all of one mind, 1 Pet. 3:8. arm yourselves likewise with the same mind, 1 Pet. 4:1. not for filthy lucre, but of a ready mind, 1 Pet. 5:2. here is the mind which hath wisdom, Rev. 17:9.",
